

Sample answer

Subject: Request to repair heating this week

Dear [Landlord’s name],

I hope you are well. I am writing to ask whether the heating in the apartment can be repaired this week. The apartment has been cold for several days, and it is becoming uncomfortable, especially at night.

Could you please let me know when a technician can come? I would be grateful if you could arrange the repair as soon as possible.

Thank you for your time and attention.

Kind regards,
[Your name]

User may adapt the email to their own situation.

Grammar explanation

  • Present perfect: “has been cold for several days” shows a situation that started in the past and continues now.
  • Modal verb: “can be repaired” is polite and formal for asking about possibility.
  • Passive voice: “can be repaired” is useful because the focus is on the repair, not on who will do it.
  • Future/request structure: “when a technician can come” asks for information politely.
  • Polite closing: “Thank you for your time and attention” is a formal way to end a business email.

